  <event id="20">
      <start>09:00</start>
      <duration>01:00</duration>
      <room>AW1.125</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Formal Dependency Management</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Debian</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Formal Dependency Management in Debian Package Repositories&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this talk we will briefly sketch the research that has been done concerning the maintenance of large package-based distributions and the formal management of inter-package dependencies, in the context of the EDOS Project.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The toolset that has been developed starting from this research will be showcased in its Debian incarnation:&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt; edos-debcheck: a dependency checker for finding inconsistencies in Debian repositories.&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt; edos-history: a package repository exploration tool that is able to handle historical Debian repositories data.&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt; anla: a web service that reports the analysis of Debian repositories over time.&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt; tart: a distribution &amp;#34;thinner&amp;#34; used to build custom Debian distributions.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA; </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="201">Berke Durak</person>
      </persons>
